1
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:22,080
2026, Tokyo. Don't brake.

2
00:00:22,130 --> 00:00:24,430
The rice balls at the convenience store got new price tags again this morning

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:26,560
The yen sets a new low every day, crashing straight through the floor

4
00:00:26,610 --> 00:00:30,100
Chairman Gao slams the table: "Found the root cause — too many foreigners!"

5
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:32,350
Permanent residency now needs a Japanese exam; nine in ten Business Manager visas vanish

6
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,250
"Orderly coexistence" in plain speech: please line up neatly… and walk far away

7
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:40,250
I say great! Whoever dares stop this acceleration is a traitor

8
00:00:40,300 --> 00:00:42,650
Prices are flying, the yen is falling

9
00:00:42,700 --> 00:00:44,950
The news says everything's fine

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:47,050
Then don't stop, don't touch the brake

11
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:51,350
Crank the volume to the max

12
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:53,750
Floor the gas, don't look back

13
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,050
Weld the doors shut, make the wall longer

14
00:00:56,100 --> 00:00:58,850
How beautiful these golden-age fireworks are

15
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:00,850
Everyone on board, sing with me

16
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:03,250
Banzai, banzai, a boundless future

17
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:05,350
Accelerate all the way, toward glory

18
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:09,550
Harder! Faster!

19
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:12,450
Hey! AI writes poetry now, and the ward office is still waiting on a fax machine

20
00:01:12,500 --> 00:01:16,250
Read the air, memorize the rules — you call it etiquette, I call it collective suffocation

21
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:19,050
Resident tax, income tax, pension — deducted on time every month, down to the last yen

22
00:01:19,100 --> 00:01:21,950
Renting starts with "your nationality?"; renewing a visa means reading every face and mood

23
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:24,150
They send us to night shifts, construction sites, and nursing care

24
00:01:24,200 --> 00:01:26,350
while cursing us online for stealing your benefits

25
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:27,450
OK, I'll leave

26
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:28,250
No hard feelings

27
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:32,250
May your rusty machine spin out a miracle soon

28
00:01:32,300 --> 00:01:34,450
Alarms are blaring, the gauges are jumping

29
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:36,750
A wall ahead — I knew it all along

30
00:01:36,800 --> 00:01:38,750
Then speed up, whatever you do, don't stop

31
00:01:38,800 --> 00:01:42,950
Push the speed to the limit

32
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,450
Faster, faster, don't stop

33
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:47,550
Throttle welded down, charging ahead

34
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:50,150
I can't wait to hear that giant crash

35
00:01:50,200 --> 00:01:52,350
Everyone on board, sing with me

36
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,550
Faster! Faster! The faster the better!

37
00:01:54,600 --> 00:01:56,850
Race wildly onward, charging into glory.

38
00:01:56,900 --> 00:02:01,450
Don't brake! Don't even think of jumping out!

39
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:06,150
Solid-state battery mass production keeps slipping; BYD is already parked outside your door

40
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:10,350
Nissan and Honda got engaged and split right away; the home-appliance supergroup is sold off and broken up

41
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,950
Trillions in chip subsidies, shouting "Rapidus will be back!"

42
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,350
Population shrinks by a whole city every year; empty houses go to auction for 1 yen

43
00:02:15,400 --> 00:02:16,450
Population decline? What the hell do I care?

44
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:17,850
The future looks grim? Not my problem

45
00:02:17,900 --> 00:02:19,550
Net-right types shouting "split the social security accounts"? Brother, that's wonderful

46
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:22,050
No more supporting your parents — my payslip just grows an extra line

47
00:02:22,100 --> 00:02:24,150
I've got a passport in my pocket, and flights leave for far away every day

48
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:29,650
When everyone who pushes wheelchairs is gone, guard your own parents' sickbeds yourselves

49
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,450
Don't stop!

50
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:35,850
That giant crash — I've waited so long.

51
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:38,350
Karma is on the way.

52
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:41,750
Don't stop (the faster the better)

53
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:44,050
Over the cliff (flying to heaven)

54
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:47,650
Till the bill arrives at your own door

55
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:50,850
Everyone sing once more — the last time

56
00:02:50,900 --> 00:02:53,450
Long live Chairman Gao, ten thousand years without end

57
00:02:53,500 --> 00:03:00,050
Vice-Chairman Xiaoyetian, forever in good health

58
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,350
Chairman Gao, long life, never stop.

59
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:04,550
Chairman Gao, long life, without end.

60
00:03:04,600 --> 00:03:06,850
Xiaoyetian, long life without end

61
00:03:06,900 --> 00:03:10,400
Vice-Chairman Xiaoyetian,

62
00:03:10,450 --> 00:03:18,880
Forever, forever healthy.

63
00:03:18,930 --> 00:03:24,590
May you run things better and better. Long life without end.

64
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:28,780
Long life without end

65
00:03:28,830 --> 00:03:31,000
Forever healthy.

